      "text": "The biological revolution unfolded across three conceptual waves: cell theory (1838-1858) established the basic unit of life; evolutionary theory (1858-1940s) explained biological diversity and change; molecular biology (1944-1970s) grounded all of biology in chemistry and information theory."
